/-!
# Classification of the ⟨1, 0, 2⟩ catalogue row

This five-atom row contains 83 isomorphism classes, listed in
[Jipsen's catalogue](https://www1.chapman.edu/~jipsen/gap/ramaddux.html).
`Model` uses zero-based indices: index `n` denotes source entry `n + 1`.
The unique-index classification expresses both exhaustiveness and absence of duplicates.
Twelve Peircean cycle orbits reduce the classification to 4096 possible cycle tables;
eight atom renamings preserve the identity and the two converse pairs.
-/

@[expose] public section

namespace Cslib.RelationAlgebra.Catalogue.I1S0N2

